<Article title="Engineering Disclaimer" description="Important limitations on the educational calculations and engineering information provided by this site." eyebrow="Safety and verification"><h2>Educational estimates</h2><p>Results are intended for learning, early design exploration, and cross-checking. They are not a substitute for device datasheets, reference manuals, protocol standards, simulation, measurement, peer review, or professional judgment.</p><h2>Model limitations</h2><p>General calculators omit conditions that can materially change a system: clock tolerance, interrupt latency, electrical behavior, errors and retransmissions, silicon errata, protocol variants, configuration modes, thermal limits, and manufacturing variation.</p><h2>Safety-critical work</h2><p>Do not rely on this site as the sole basis for medical, automotive safety, aerospace, industrial protection, mains-connected, or other safety-critical decisions. Apply the standards, analysis methods, validation, and competent review required for your field.</p><h2>Your responsibility</h2><p>Check entered units and assumptions, independently reproduce important results, and test the implemented system under normal, boundary, and fault conditions.</p></Article>
